{% comment %}
  ==================================================================
  GS COLLECTION FILTERS
  Ported from gs-shopify-v3 snippets/collection-filters.liquid (32.6 KB)
  ==================================================================
  Owns the FiltersForm that gs-collection-toolbar's sort radios submit
  to via form="FiltersForm". Used by main-collection AND main-search.

  USAGE:
    render 'gs-collection-filters', section: section, sort_by: sort_by

  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  REVISION 2026-08-13 - THREE FIXES, ALL FROM THE PORT NOT FROM v3
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  1. COLOUR FILTERS RENDERED AS TEXT CHECKBOXES, NOT SWATCHES.
     Swatch detection read `settings.custom_colors_options` - a v3 THEME
     SETTING with no entry in Dawn's config/settings_schema.json. It was
     nil, so is_color was always false.

     Detection now works from data Shopify actually provides:
       - filter.presentation is 'swatch' or 'image'
       - or any value carries a swatch colour or image
       - or the filter label looks like a colour filter
     The v3 setting is still honoured if it is ever added.

  2. "CLEAR ALL" LINKED NOWHERE ON THE SEARCH PAGE.
     href was collection.url, and there is no collection on /search, so
     the link resolved to an empty string. Now falls back to the search
     URL carrying the current term.

  3. THE NO-JS PATH LOST THE SEARCH TERM.
     The hidden `q` input only rendered when collection.terms existed.
     On /search that is nil, so submitting the form without JavaScript
     dropped the query. gs-collection-filter.js already carried `q` for
     the AJAX path; the plain submit did not.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  DUPLICATE DOM IDs ON EVERY COLLECTION PAGE (v3)
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  v3's main-collection rendered BOTH the topbar and this snippet, each
  containing a full sort control, both emitting id="sort__list" and
  sortByOption-1..N. Duplicate ids break label[for] association -
  clicking a sort label can focus the wrong radio. The sidebar copy is
  deleted; gs-collection-toolbar owns sort.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  GLOBAL CSS FROM A PRICE-SLIDER TUTORIAL (v3)
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
      .wrapper { width: 400px; background: #fff; }
      header h2 { font-size: 24px; font-weight: 600; }
      header p  { margin-top: 5px; font-size: 16px; }
      ::selection { color: #fff; background: #ab192d; }

  `header h2` and `header p` are element selectors that hit the SITE
  HEADER, from a snippet that only renders on collection pages. None
  carried over; everything is namespaced under .gs-filters.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  PRICE FILTER: TWO REAL v3 BUGS
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  1. `assign maxpricevalue = min_value` - the slider's max handle was
     computed from the MINIMUM in the comma-decimal branch.
  2. The MAX price input's value was guarded by the MIN value, so
     filtering by maximum price only left the To field visually empty
     even though the filter applied. That one affects USD.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  OTHER v3 FIXES
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  - ids were built from human labels, producing id="FilterProduct type1"
    - a space in an id is invalid and breaks label[for]. Handleized.
  - ~12 KB of commented-out code, an entire duplicate topbar. Liquid
    still tokenizes comment bodies, so it cost parse time per page.
  - has_active for price_range used AND, so a min-only filter did not
    count as active and its group would not auto-open.
  - Three <a> elements with no href served as close buttons.
  - snippets/swatchs-filter (misspelled) inlined; it was 1.1 KB.
  ==================================================================
{% endcomment %}

{{ 'gs-collection-filters.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- liquid
  # Search and collection share this snippet.
  assign is_search = false
  if search.performed
    assign is_search = true
  endif

  assign filter_set = collection.filters
  if is_search
    assign filter_set = search.filters
  endif

  assign clear_url = collection.url
  if is_search
    assign clear_url = routes.search_url | append: '?q=' | append: search.terms | url_encode
  endif

  # Kept in case the v3 setting is ever added to settings_schema.json.
  assign color_option_labels = settings.custom_colors_options | downcase | default: 'color,colour,colorway,colourway'

  # PATTERN_SWATCH: v3 hardcoded this CDN URL inline for any filter value
  # labelled 'Pattern'. Kept so the swatch keeps working; it should become
  # a real Shopify swatch on the option value.
  assign pattern_swatch_url = 'https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0703/2002/9955/files/Web_Site_Color_Swatch_USAFlagANDRedWhiteBlue_1_-min_1.jpg?v=1768337863'

  assign comma_decimal_currencies = 'ANG,ARS,BRL,BYN,BYR,CLF,CLP,COP,CRC,CZK,DKK,EUR,HRK,HUF,IDR,ISK,MZN,NOK,PLN,RON,RUB,SEK,TRY,UYU,VES,VND' | split: ','
  assign uses_comma_decimals = false
  if comma_decimal_currencies contains cart.currency.iso_code
    assign uses_comma_decimals = true
  endif
-%}

<div class="gs-filters" id="GsCollectionFilters-{{ section.id }}" data-side-drawer>
  <form id="FiltersForm" class="gs-filters__form" data-form-id>
    <div class="gs-filters__head">
      <p class="gs-filters__title">
        <svg width="18" height="16" viewBox="0 0 12 11" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
          <path d="M0 9.77778L8.21516e-08 8.55556H2.53875V7.33333H4.23125V8.55556H11.8475V9.77778H4.23125V11H2.53875V9.77778H0ZM2.46314e-07 6.11111L3.28396e-07 4.88889H7.61625V3.66667H9.30876V4.88889H11.8475V6.11111H9.30876V7.33333H7.61625V6.11111H2.46314e-07ZM4.92629e-07 2.44444L5.7471e-07 1.22223H2.53875V0L4.23125 4.80826e-08V1.22223H11.8475V2.44444H4.23125V3.66667H2.53875V2.44444H4.92629e-07Z" fill="currentColor"/>
        </svg>
        {{ 'sections.collection_template.filter_by_label' | t }}
      </p>

      <button
        type="button"
        class="gs-filters__close"
        aria-label="{{ 'accessibility.close' | t }}"
        data-side-drawer-close
      >
        <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 10 10" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
          <path d="M8.99998 0L9.99998 0.999969L0.999998 9.99969L0 8.99972L8.99998 0Z" fill="currentColor"/>
          <path d="M2.39302e-05 1.00028L1.00002 0.000307701L10 9.00003L9 10L2.39302e-05 1.00028Z" fill="currentColor"/>
        </svg>
      </button>
    </div>

    <div class="gs-filters__body">
      {%- comment -%}
        The search term must ride along or a no-JS submit loses it.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if is_search -%}
        <input type="hidden" name="q" value="{{ search.terms | escape }}">
        <input type="hidden" name="options[prefix]" value="last">
      {%- elsif collection.terms -%}
        <input type="hidden" name="q" value="{{ collection.terms | escape }}">
        <input type="hidden" name="options[prefix]" value="last">
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if collection.current_vendor or collection.current_type -%}
        <input type="hidden" name="q" value="{{ collection.current_vendor }}{{ collection.current_type }}">
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- for filter in filter_set -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign filter_label = filter.label
          assign filter_label_down = filter_label | downcase
          assign filter_key = filter.param_name | default: filter_label | handleize

          # Swatch detection from data Shopify provides, not from a v3
          # theme setting that does not exist here.
          assign is_color = false
          if filter.presentation == 'swatch' or filter.presentation == 'image'
            assign is_color = true
          elsif color_option_labels contains filter_label_down
            assign is_color = true
          else
            for probe in filter.values limit: 1
              if probe.swatch.color or probe.swatch.image
                assign is_color = true
              endif
            endfor
          endif

          assign has_active = false
          if filter.type == 'price_range'
            if filter.min_value.value != null or filter.max_value.value != null
              assign has_active = true
            endif
          else
            if filter.active_values.size > 0
              assign has_active = true
            endif
          endif

          assign should_open = false
          if has_active
            assign should_open = true
          elsif section.settings.open_all_filtering
            assign should_open = true
          elsif section.settings.open_filtering and forloop.first
            assign should_open = true
          endif
        -%}

        <details
          class="gs-filters__group"
          data-filter-key="{{ filter_key }}"
          {% if should_open %}open{% endif %}
        >
          <summary class="gs-filters__group-title" data-filter-label="{{ filter_label | escape }}">
            {{- filter_label -}}
            <svg class="gs-filters__chevron" width="12" height="8" viewBox="0 0 12 8" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
              <path d="M11 1L6 6L1 1" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/>
            </svg>
          </summary>

          <div class="gs-filters__group-body">
            {%- case filter.type -%}

              {%- when 'boolean', 'list' -%}
                <ul class="gs-filters__values list-unstyled{% if is_color %} gs-filters__values--swatch{% endif %}">
                  {%- for filter_value in filter.values -%}
                    {%- liquid
                      assign value_id = 'Filter-' | append: section.id | append: '-' | append: filter_key | append: '-' | append: forloop.index

                      assign is_disabled = false
                      if filter_value.count == 0 and filter_value.active == false and is_color == false
                        assign is_disabled = true
                      endif

                      assign swatch_style = ''
                      if filter_value.label == 'Pattern'
                        capture swatch_style
                          echo 'background: url(' | append: pattern_swatch_url | append: ') no-repeat center center / cover;'
                        endcapture
                      elsif filter_value.swatch.color
                        capture swatch_style
                          echo 'background-color: ' | append: filter_value.swatch.color | append: ';'
                        endcapture
                      elsif filter_value.swatch.image
                        assign swatch_image_url = filter_value.swatch.image | image_url: width: 100
                        capture swatch_style
                          echo 'background: url(' | append: swatch_image_url | append: ') no-repeat center center / cover;'
                        endcapture
                      endif
                    -%}

                    <li class="gs-filters__value{% if is_color %} gs-filters__value--swatch{% endif %}{% if is_disabled %} is-disabled{% endif %}">
                      <input
                        type="checkbox"
                        class="gs-filters__checkbox"
                        name="{{ filter_value.param_name }}"
                        value="{{ filter_value.value }}"
                        id="{{ value_id }}"
                        {% if filter_value.active %}checked{% endif %}
                        {% if is_disabled %}disabled{% endif %}
                      >
                      <label class="gs-filters__label" for="{{ value_id }}" title="{{ filter_value.label | escape }}">
                        {%- if is_color -%}
                          {%- comment -%}
                            Inlined from snippets/swatchs-filter (misspelled
                            in v3). The visible name lives in a
                            visually-hidden span so the swatch keeps an
                            accessible name.
                          {%- endcomment -%}
                          <span class="gs-filters__swatch" style="{{ swatch_style }}" data-color="{{ filter_value.label | escape | downcase }}"></span>
                          <span class="visually-hidden">{{ filter_value.label | escape }} ({{ filter_value.count }})</span>
                        {%- else -%}
                          <span class="gs-filters__tick" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                          <span class="gs-filters__value-name">{{ filter_value.label | escape }}</span>
                          <span class="gs-filters__count">({{ filter_value.count }})</span>
                        {%- endif -%}
                      </label>
                    </li>
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </ul>

              {%- when 'price_range' -%}
                {%- liquid
                  if uses_comma_decimals
                    assign range_min_raw = filter.range_min | money_without_currency | replace: '.', '' | replace: ',', '.' | floor
                    assign range_max_raw = filter.range_max | money_without_currency | replace: '.', '' | replace: ',', '.' | floor
                  else
                    assign range_min_raw = filter.range_min | money_without_currency | replace: ',', '' | floor
                    assign range_max_raw = filter.range_max | money_without_currency | replace: ',', '' | floor
                  endif

                  assign min_current = range_min_raw
                  assign max_current = range_max_raw

                  if filter.min_value.value
                    if uses_comma_decimals
                      assign min_current = filter.min_value.value | money_without_currency | replace: '.', '' | replace: ',', '.' | floor
                    else
                      assign min_current = filter.min_value.value | money_without_currency | replace: ',', '' | floor
                    endif
                  endif

                  if filter.max_value.value
                    if uses_comma_decimals
                      assign max_current = filter.max_value.value | money_without_currency | replace: '.', '' | replace: ',', '.' | floor
                    else
                      assign max_current = filter.max_value.value | money_without_currency | replace: ',', '' | floor
                    endif
                  endif

                  assign progress_left = 0
                  assign progress_right = 0
                  if range_max_raw > 0
                    assign progress_left = min_current | times: 100.0 | divided_by: range_max_raw
                    assign progress_right_used = max_current | times: 100.0 | divided_by: range_max_raw
                    assign progress_right = 100 | minus: progress_right_used
                  endif

                  assign gte_id = 'Filter-' | append: section.id | append: '-' | append: filter_key | append: '-GTE'
                  assign lte_id = 'Filter-' | append: section.id | append: '-' | append: filter_key | append: '-LTE'
                -%}

                <div class="gs-filters__price">
                  <div class="gs-filters__slider">
                    <div
                      class="gs-filters__slider-progress"
                      style="left: {{ progress_left | at_least: 0 }}%; right: {{ progress_right | at_least: 0 }}%;"
                    ></div>
                  </div>

                  <div class="gs-filters__range no-js-hidden" data-target="price">
                    <input
                      type="range"
                      class="gs-filters__range-input gs-filters__range-input--min"
                      min="{{ range_min_raw }}"
                      max="{{ range_max_raw }}"
                      value="{{ min_current }}"
                      step="1"
                      aria-label="{{ 'sections.collection_template.from' | t }}"
                    >
                    <input
                      type="range"
                      class="gs-filters__range-input gs-filters__range-input--max"
                      min="{{ range_min_raw }}"
                      max="{{ range_max_raw }}"
                      value="{{ max_current }}"
                      step="1"
                      aria-label="{{ 'sections.collection_template.to' | t }}"
                    >
                  </div>

                  <div class="gs-filters__price-fields">
                    <div class="gs-filters__field">
                      <label class="gs-filters__field-name" for="{{ gte_id }}">
                        {{ 'sections.collection_template.from' | t }}
                      </label>
                      <div class="gs-filters__field-wrap">
                        <span class="gs-filters__currency">{{ cart.currency.symbol }}</span>
                        <input
                          class="gs-filters__field-input"
                          name="{{ filter.min_value.param_name }}"
                          id="{{ gte_id }}"
                          type="number"
                          inputmode="numeric"
                          min="0"
                          max="{{ range_max_raw }}"
                          placeholder="{{ range_min_raw }}"
                          {% if filter.min_value.value %}value="{{ min_current }}"{% endif %}
                        >
                      </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="gs-filters__field">
                      <label class="gs-filters__field-name" for="{{ lte_id }}">
                        {{ 'sections.collection_template.to' | t }}
                      </label>
                      <div class="gs-filters__field-wrap">
                        <span class="gs-filters__currency">{{ cart.currency.symbol }}</span>
                        <input
                          class="gs-filters__field-input"
                          name="{{ filter.max_value.param_name }}"
                          id="{{ lte_id }}"
                          type="number"
                          inputmode="numeric"
                          min="0"
                          max="{{ range_max_raw }}"
                          placeholder="{{ range_max_raw }}"
                          {%- comment -%}
                            v3 guarded this with filter.min_value.value, so
                            a max-only price filter left the field empty.
                          {%- endcomment -%}
                          {% if filter.max_value.value %}value="{{ max_current }}"{% endif %}
                        >
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>

            {%- endcase -%}
          </div>
        </details>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>

    <div class="gs-filters__actions">
      <button type="submit" class="button btn-block gs-filters__submit">
        {{ 'sections.collection_template.show_results' | t }}
      </button>
      <a class="gs-filters__clear" href="{{ clear_url }}">
        {{ 'sections.collection_template.clear_all' | t }}
      </a>
    </div>
  </form>
</div>
